    "comment": "Seke (Vanuatu) (1465-ske) = Threatened (100 percent certain, based on the evidence available) (Language shift is occurring in the northern and southern extremes of Seke territory where speakers are switching to Bislama and either Apma or Sa. In the sparsely populated region at the heart of Seke territory, the language is still quite strong. Even in the northern and southern extremes, children often still learn Seke.) [Johnson 2014](cldf:johnson:14)"
